  <!-- ============ SECTION 1 ============ -->
  
  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="card ci">
      <div class="callout warn">REGULATORY STATUS (as previously confirmed in the earlier individual Lagebericht poster): Germany has not yet transposed the EU's CSRD into national law. §§315b–315c below reflect the ORIGINAL 2017 regime, which remains operative for now. Verify current status before relying on this for a live filing.</div>

  
      <div class="ctitle ci">The final Titel of the Konzernabschluss subsection</div>
      <div class="principle">§§315–315d close out Book 3, Section 2's Konzernabschluss subsection, mirroring the earlier individual-entity Lagebericht (§§289–289f) but scaled to the GROUP as a whole. As with the Konzernanhang poster, this poster focuses genuine attention on what is DISTINCTIVELY group-level here — multi-entity financial risk management disclosure, and the duplicate-reporting exemption for a subsidiary already covered by its own parent's group statement.</div>
      <div class="elabel">HOW §§315–315D MAP TO GERMAN ACCOUNTING PRINCIPLES</div>
      <div class="check-list">
        <span><strong>Ein den tatsächlichen Verhältnissen entsprechendes Bild</strong> — the SAME true-and-fair formulation reappears here, now describing the GROUP's own course of business and position</span>
        <span><strong>Avoiding duplicate reporting</strong> — the SAME theme running through §264(3), §291/§292, and §315b(2)'s own subsidiary exemption</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card cs">
      <div class="ctitle cs">What §§315–315d require, at a glance</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th cols-06-17"><span>§</span><span>Core requirement</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-06-17"><span>315</span><span>Group course of business, position, forecast, risks/opportunities, financial risk management</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-06-17"><span>315a</span><span>Takeover-related disclosures for certain listed parent AGs/KGaAs</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-06-17"><span>315b–c</span><span>Non-financial group statement obligation and content, with a duplicate-avoidance exemption</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-06-17"><span>315d</span><span>Group corporate governance statement for listed parents</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 2 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">Every parent required to prepare a Konzernabschluss under §290</div>
      <div class="principle">§315's core content requirements apply to every parent required to prepare a Konzernlagebericht under §290(1)'s obligation established many posters ago. §315a, §315b, and §315d each add progressively narrower layers, reaching only listed parent AGs/KGaAs or large capital-market-oriented groups exceeding 500 employees.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 3 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>§315(1) — the Core Content Test, at Group Level</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">The same requirement as §289(1), now describing the entire group</div>
      <div class="principle">§315(1) requires the Konzernlagebericht to present the course of business — including the business result — and the POSITION of the GROUP, such that a picture corresponding to actual circumstances is conveyed, together with an accurate presentation of the principal opportunities and risks of expected future development, an assessment and explanation of that development, and disclosure of the material assumptions underlying any forward-looking statements — the SAME Prognosebericht requirement established in the individual-entity poster, now assessed on a consolidated, group-wide basis.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 4 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Worked Example — a Group-Level Prognosebericht</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2">
      <div class="ctitle cs">Assumptions must be disclosed for the GROUP's combined outlook</div>
      <div class="worked">
        <div class="wk-title">Example 1: A group's combined outlook statement</div>
        <div class="wk-body">A group comprising a manufacturing parent and a distribution subsidiary expects combined revenue growth of 8% in the coming year, based on assumed continued expansion in the subsidiary's distribution network and stable input costs at the parent's own manufacturing operations.</div>
        <div class="wk-answer">The Konzernlagebericht must disclose BOTH underlying assumptions explicitly — the distribution network expansion and the stable input cost assumption — exactly as §289(1) required at the individual-entity level, but now describing the COMBINED, group-wide picture rather than either entity's own outlook in isolation.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 5 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>§315(2) — Further Required Content, Including Financial Risk Management</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">The same four categories as §289(2), plus genuinely heightened financial risk management content</div>
      <div class="principle">§315(2) carries forward the SAME four categories established for the individual Lagebericht — subsequent events of particular significance, expected development with opportunities/risks, R&amp;D activities, and existing branches — now assessed group-wide. Groups with more complex, multi-entity treasury and hedging operations spanning several legal entities typically also address the enterprise's RISK MANAGEMENT OBJECTIVES AND METHODS relating to the use of financial instruments — currency, interest rate, credit, and liquidity risk exposures that are often genuinely more significant, and more genuinely GROUP-WIDE in character, than at any single entity in isolation.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 6 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — Disclosing Group-Wide Treasury and Hedging Risk</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">A genuinely group-wide exposure, managed centrally</div>
      <div class="worked">
        <div class="wk-title">Example 2: A centralised group treasury function</div>
        <div class="wk-body">A group's central treasury function, based at the parent, manages foreign currency risk on behalf of ALL group entities, using forward contracts to hedge a combined €40,000,000 of exposure arising from multiple subsidiaries' own foreign-denominated receivables and payables.</div>
        <div class="wk-answer">The Konzernlagebericht discloses the group's OVERALL currency risk management objectives and methods — describing the centralised hedging approach, the combined €40,000,000 exposure, and the general hedging instruments used — rather than each individual subsidiary separately describing its OWN, comparatively narrow slice of the SAME centrally-managed risk.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 7 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>§315(3)–(5) — Non-Financial Indicators and the Group Accounting Process Controls</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">The same narrower forerunner content, now describing the Konzernrechnungslegungsprozess</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">§315(3) requires non-financial performance indicators relevant to understanding the GROUP's business to be included, to the extent necessary — the SAME requirement as §289(3), assessed group-wide. §315(4)–(5) require, for capital-market-oriented PARENTS specifically, a description of the main characteristics of the internal control and risk management system as it relates to the GROUP accounting process (Konzernrechnungslegungsprozess) — a genuinely more complex environment than any single entity's own accounting process, given the additional consolidation-specific controls (uniform measurement, elimination entries, capital consolidation mechanics) this entire poster series has documented.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 8 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>§315a — Takeover-Related Disclosures, Now at Group Level</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">The same substantive content as §289a, delivered through the group report</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">§315a requires the SAME substantive takeover-related disclosures established under §289a — share capital composition, voting/transfer restrictions, 10%+ shareholdings, special control rights, board appointment/removal rules, share issuance/buyback powers, and change-of-control clauses in material agreements — now delivered through the Konzernlagebericht where the PARENT itself is a listed AG or KGaA.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 9 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>§315b — the Non-Financial Group Statement Obligation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">The same 500-employee, capital-market-oriented threshold, assessed group-wide</div>
      <div class="principle">§315b(1) requires a parent meeting the SAME criteria established for the individual-entity §289b obligation — in practice, capital-market-oriented groups (and certain credit institutions/insurers) exceeding 500 employees, assessed on a GROUP-WIDE basis — to expand the Konzernlagebericht with a non-financial GROUP statement, covering the same five topics: environmental, employee, social, human rights, and anti-corruption/anti-bribery matters.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 10 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>§315b(2) — Avoiding Duplicate Non-Financial Reporting Within a Group</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">The same "avoid duplication" theme, applied to non-financial reporting specifically</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">§315b(2) exempts a subsidiary from preparing its OWN separate non-financial statement (whether at individual-entity level under §289b, or at its own sub-group level under §315b) where it is ITSELF already included within a PARENT's own non-financial group statement — directly paralleling the SAME duplicate-avoidance logic already seen for financial reporting under §264(3) (individual-entity subsidiary exemption) and §291/§292 (group-level exemption for EU/EEA and third-country sub-groups).</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 11 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example — a Subsidiary Relying on the §315b(2) Exemption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2">
      <div class="ctitle cs">Genuine relief within a nested group, once again</div>
      <div class="worked">
        <div class="wk-title">Example 3: A German sub-group within a larger, non-financial-reporting parent group</div>
        <div class="wk-body">A German intermediate parent, itself a capital-market-oriented company exceeding 500 employees on its own sub-group basis, is wholly owned by a larger European parent whose own non-financial group statement — covering the SAME five topics — fully incorporates the German sub-group's own operations.</div>
        <div class="wk-answer">The German intermediate parent relies on §315b(2) to be EXEMPTED from preparing its OWN separate non-financial group statement — its environmental, employee, social, human rights, and anti-corruption information remains fully visible through the LARGER parent's own group-wide non-financial statement, avoiding a substantively duplicative reporting exercise, exactly paralleling the financial-reporting exemptions established much earlier in this series.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 12 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>§315c — Content of the Non-Financial Group Statement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">The same content structure as §289c, assessed group-wide</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">§315c requires the SAME content structure established under §289c — a description of the group's business model, and for each of the five topics, its concepts pursued, due diligence processes, outcomes, principal risks connected with the group's own operations and its business relationships/products/services, how those risks are managed, and relevant non-financial KPIs — now assessed across the ENTIRE group rather than a single entity, meaning the due diligence and risk assessment must genuinely span the group's own supply chains and business relationships wherever they sit within the corporate structure.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 13 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>§315d — the Group Corporate Governance Statement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">The same content as §289f, for the parent's own governance arrangements</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">§315d requires listed parent AGs to include a group corporate governance statement — covering the German Corporate Governance Code declaration of conformity, governance practices applied beyond legal requirements, the working methods of the PARENT's own management and supervisory boards and their committees, and diversity-related board composition information — mirroring §289f's individual-entity content, since the group itself has no separate governing body distinct from the parent's own.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 14 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Practical Difficulties</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div>
          <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
          <div class="dot-list">
            <span>Whether centrally-managed financial risk genuinely warrants group-wide disclosure treatment versus entity-by-entity description</span>
            <span>Whether a subsidiary's own non-financial matters are GENUINELY fully captured within a parent's own group statement, justifying the §315b(2) exemption</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="elabel">PRACTICAL DIFFICULTIES</div>
          <div class="dot-list">
            <span>Coordinating group-wide due diligence and risk assessment across a complex, multi-entity, multi-jurisdictional supply chain for §315c purposes</span>
            <span>The SAME CSRD transposition uncertainty flagged in the individual Lagebericht poster, now affecting an even broader population of groups once eventual transposition occurs</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 15 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — HGB §§315–315d vs IFRS</div>
      <div class="text-supporting">Exactly as with the individual Lagebericht, the Konzernlagebericht as a WHOLE remains one of the most distinctively non-IFRS components of this entire poster series — IFRS financial statements embed no mandatory, statutorily-defined forecast narrative at either the individual OR the group level. Where a group prepares BOTH an HGB Konzernabschluss and separately reports under IFRS (e.g. a listed parent using §315e, covered in the next poster), the Konzernlagebericht's forward-looking, risk-and-opportunity content remains a genuinely ADDITIONAL, HGB-specific requirement layered on top of whatever IFRS itself requires.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 16 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2">
      <div class="ctitle cs">Where every §§315–315d event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event / obligation</span><span>Document affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Group Prognosebericht content</span><span><span class="badge bo">Konzernlagebericht</span></span><span>Outside the Konzernabschluss definition entirely</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Non-financial group statement (§315b)</span><span><span class="badge bo">Konzernlagebericht</span> (or standalone report)</span><span>Subject to the §315b(2) duplicate-avoidance exemption</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Group governance statement (§315d)</span><span><span class="badge bo">Konzernlagebericht</span></span><span>Listed parent AGs only</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 17 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Related Provisions — Cross-Reference Map</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">How §§315–315d connect across HGB Book 3</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Provision</span><span>Nature of the connection</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>§289–289f</span><span>The individual-entity Lagebericht provisions this Titel closely parallels at group level</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>§290(1)</span><span>Establishes the Konzernlagebericht obligation this Titel now fills with substantive content</span></div>
        <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>§264(3), §291, §292</span><span>The earlier duplicate-avoidance exemptions §315b(2) directly parallels for non-financial reporting specifically</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>§315e</span><span>The NEXT and final Titel in this Subsection, permitting IFRS group accounts as an alternative to the entire Konzernabschluss/Konzernlagebericht framework</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 18 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s18"><span class="num">18</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Konzernlagebericht</div><div class="glossary-def">Group management report — the consolidated equivalent of the individual-entity Lagebericht, kept outside the Konzernabschluss definition.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Konzernrechnungslegungsprozess</div><div class="glossary-def">The group accounting process — the internal control environment specifically covering consolidation mechanics, disclosed under §315(4)-(5).</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Finanzrisikomanagement</div><div class="glossary-def">Financial risk management — currency, interest rate, credit, and liquidity risk disclosure, often genuinely group-wide given centralised treasury functions.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Nichtfinanzielle Konzernerklärung</div><div class="glossary-def">Non-financial group statement — the group-wide equivalent of the individual non-financial statement under §289b.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Key</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bo">Konzernlagebericht</span> Group management report
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
